## Feasibility (raid 91a35c): WARN, workable

Mechanical check of every reference above against 998cd705: all files,
functions and tests exist; line ranges are right to within a few lines
(comments precede `worktree_scrub` at 113-115 and the gc guard call at
253-256). No caller in `profiles/`, `agents/`, `commands/`, `Makefile`,
`.github/`, `bin/`, `ci-local/` or hooks. For the coder:

- `worktree-clean-lib.sh:77-78` calls status with `--ignored=matching`:
  the rewrite drops that flag explicitly; a copied call keeps the old rule.
- Inverted tests take names that say the new outcome:
  `test_preflight_blocks_on_ignored_draft_under_star_ignore` (779), the
  `ignored-draft` case of `test_uv_venv_does_not_mask_real_work` (1583),
  `test_gc_keeps_idle_ownerless_tree_holding_ignored_files` (1770).
- Not classified above, in `tests/test_worktree_tools.py`: 169
  `test_hunt_tmp_exclude_registration_uses_shared_git_metadata` (register:
  keep), 1319 `test_removal_preflight_refused_by_residue_keeps_panel` (read
  it against the `preserve_panel` deletion), 1392 and 1408 (preflight
  argument handling: keep).
- `skills/roar/close-and-clean.sh:219` and `skills/lair/SKILL.md:52` call the
  plain preflight and stay; lair's "uncommitted/untracked" wording becomes
